<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    v0.41.0: the MindAnchor mark.

    The previous foreground was a literal anchor on a dusk-sky gradient.
    Anchors are easy marks to over-reach for in apps with "anchor" in
    the name; the result is usually a clip-art silhouette. A Red Dot
    2025 jury reads the difference between a literal symbol and an
    abstract mark. The new foreground is a single circle with a small
    inner dot, drawn in sage on a warm cream paper background.

    The mark is the same one the v0.38.0 breathing surface draws: a
    breath circle with a point of stillness at its centre. The
    launcher icon and the breathing surface are now the same
    picture. The app grid and the screen behind the breath are the
    same room.

    Geometry notes, because an adaptive icon is easy to get subtly
    wrong and impossible to check by reading:

    The canvas is 108x108dp but only the central 66dp is guaranteed
    visible — every launcher masks the rest and some crop hard. The
    circle at radius 28 sits well inside that, with stroke 6 (one
    unit past the ring sits at radius 31, still inside). The inner
    dot is radius 6, drawn filled in the same sage so the eye reads
    "circle with a point of stillness" rather than "ring with a hole."

    The previous 5/7 unit stroke was the right call for the literal
    anchor; the new foreground is a single circle, which wants a
    slightly heavier stroke (6) to read as deliberate at 48dp. Too
    thin and the circle looks like a wire; too thick and it looks
    like a wheel. 6 is the diameter/9 ratio that holds at 48, 72,
    and 108dp.

    Round line caps, no sharp points, in keeping with an app that
    avoids anything that reads as an alarm.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- The breath circle. Stroke only; the interior is the
         warm cream paper from the background layer showing through. -->
    <path
        android:strokeColor="#57726A"
        android:strokeWidth="6"
        android:fillColor="@android:color/transparent"
        android:pathData="M 54 26 A 28 28 0 1 1 54 82 A 28 28 0 1 1 54 26 Z" />

    <!-- The point of stillness at the centre. Filled in the
         same sage so the eye reads it as part of the mark, not
         as a separate element. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#57726A"
        android:pathData="M 54 48 A 6 6 0 1 1 54 60 A 6 6 0 1 1 54 48 Z" />
</vector>
